WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.018 --> 00:00:03.030
(siren wails)

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.210
- [Reporter] Since February 24th, 2022,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.250
when Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.340
announced a special military operation,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.340
the West has walked a
fine line in Ukraine.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.835
(soft tense music)

00:00:15.835 --> 00:00:17.370
(mother cries)

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.960
While it works to help Ukraine

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.761
push back the Russian invasion,

00:00:20.761 --> 00:00:23.490
(rockets hiss)

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.850
Western countries are also
carefully calculating their aid

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.460
to avoid getting pulled
into a direct conflict

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.593
with a nuclear armed adversary.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.640
The "Wall Street Journal"
examined Western military aid

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.760
over the first year of
the Russia Ukraine War

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.350
to see what's next.

00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:44.340
(soft tense music ends)

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.750
The war over the last year can
be broken into three phases.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.550
- Initially, the Ukrainians were looking

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.840
for almost anything.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.700
I mean, one thing they requested early on,

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.220
which didn't happen, was that the US

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.240
and NATO impose a no-fly
zone over Ukrainian airspace.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.500
- [Reporter] That was a red line

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.823
the West didn't want to
cross and still hasn't

00:01:04.823 --> 00:01:09.086
- [Protesters] Close the sky,
close the sky, close the sky.

00:01:09.086 --> 00:01:10.460
- [Reporter] But they
were providing other gear.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.770
- I'd say the first phase with
the sort of insurgency phase

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.860
and the anti-tank weapons,
you know, small arms

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.870
and essentially meant for,

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.020
you know, what would likely
to be partisan warfare.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.880
- [Reporter] A few days
after the invasion,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.820
Germany announced it would
send Ukraine anti-tank weapons

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.340
and Stinger missiles, a stark difference

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.370
from its previous legislation
banning the delivery of arms

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.080
to conflict regions.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.120
And in March, Germany also added

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.440
2,700 anti-aircraft missiles to that list.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.730
By the end of the month,

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.030
officials of the Ukrainian
army were touting wins.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:48.810
Russian forces began pulling
back from Kyiv and Chernihiv.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.771
By Wednesday, April 6th,
that withdrawal was complete.

00:01:52.771 --> 00:01:55.188
(soft music)

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.940
But with a renewed Russian
offensive in Eastern Ukraine,

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.110
the US had announced another
$800 million package of aid.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.810
In that package were M777 Howitzers...

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:07.766
- [Officer] Fire!

00:02:07.766 --> 00:02:09.930
(ammunition fires)

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.010
- [Reporter] Artillery pieces

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:14.264
that can provide long-range
fire support from the rear.

00:02:14.264 --> 00:02:16.860
(artillery rumbles)

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.680
And as fighting shifted to
an attempted all-out assault

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.140
by Russian forces in the Donbas area,

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.300
Ukrainian officials
stressed the urgent need

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.810
for even more sophisticated
long-range weaponry.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.440
The US responded, this time
with advanced rocket systems

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.912
like these that transitioned
the war into a new phase.

00:02:34.912 --> 00:02:37.050
(rockets roar)

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.790
Ukraine also began securing

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.670
this kind of high mobility
artillery rocket systems,

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.300
known as HIMARS, and multiple
launch rocket systems

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.699
similar to these, or MLRs.

00:02:47.699 --> 00:02:50.910
(rockets hiss)

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:53.250
As the war passed 100 days,

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.710
Russian forces were
consolidating their position

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.170
toward the south and east of the country,

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.970
looking to expand their control

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.550
to strategic cities like this one.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.050
The arrival of these HIMARS

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.470
helped strengthen Kyiv's
hand in these areas,

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:11.010
but these types of new weapons
came with a clear red line.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.110
- Attacking occupied
territory is one thing,

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:16.080
but we don't want you
using our artillery systems

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.420
to attack targets in Russia.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.450
And that's one reason why
the US has been reluctant,

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.180
in fact, hasn't delivered
longer range artillery

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.700
or longer range ammunition
that could be used

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.760
in the HIMARS because it
doesn't want the Ukrainians

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.170
to be attacking Russia.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.510
- [Reporter] To ensure this
line and reduce the risk

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.750
of a wider war with Moscow,
the US secretly modified

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.990
the advanced HIMAR rocket
launchers it gave Ukraine.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.510
The Pentagon declined to
comment on the modifications,

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.190
which US officials said involved

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.753
their hardware and software.

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:49.020
By the sixth month of war in Ukraine,

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.200
momentum tilted against Russia's favor,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.060
shown clearly with this drone strike

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.630
on the headquarters of Russia's
Black Sea fleet in Crimea.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.780
Still, the US announced
another nearly $3 billion

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.070
for Ukraine's defense,

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:06.270
the biggest US weapons
assistance package thus far.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.550
Ukraine made advances throughout the fall,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.670
first in Kharkiv, then in Kherson.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.600
Russian forces pulled back
from Kharkiv in September.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.040
Ukraine said it had retaken

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.160
about 3,500 square miles of territory

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.320
from Moscow forces in the region.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.720
This marks the biggest setback for Russia

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.170
since it invaded Ukraine in
February, and in November,

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:31.260
Russia ordered the withdrawal
of its troops from Kherson,

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:34.327
the only regional
Ukrainian capital it held.

00:04:34.327 --> 00:04:37.410
(protesters singing)

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.620
As winter set with cold
weather and shorter days,

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.083
both sides slowed down their war efforts.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:49.200
But in 2023, a renewed push
for military aid ramped up.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.810
Tanks like these kicked
off the most recent phase

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.660
of military aid and marked a departure

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.340
from previous policies.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.660
- Early on in the war,

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:01.080
the thought of sending
Western battle tanks

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.590
would be sort of regarded as
really being a very risky step

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.940
and a step too far.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:09.210
Now, of course, they're
about to go into the theater.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.340
- [Reporter] It began
with the UK agreeing first

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.620
to send Western battle tanks to Ukraine

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.680
followed by the US providing
Abrams tanks like these

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.150
and Germany outlining plans

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.190
to send Leopard tanks like these ones.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:23.580
- The Russians have massed
large numbers of forces

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.460
and pushed them into
Ukraine, leading Western

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.300
and Ukrainian analysts to expect
a further Russian offensive

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.970
because the Russians seem
to be playing for time.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:35.310
You know, it seems like
they want a long war.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.610
They're waiting for something
to turn up in their favor.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.750
- [Reporter] While the tanks will increase

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.640
the Ukrainians' combat power,

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.220
that equipment is some ways off.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.560
And further constraints on Western aid

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.420
loom as the war carries on.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.760
- Western supplies are not limitless.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.110
The ability of Western industry

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.660
to kind of produce more equipment

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.540
for their own armies to
replace the equipment

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.240
that's been sent to Ukraine and also more

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.870
for the Ukrainians themselves,
it isn't limitless.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.840
- [Reporter] The US has
committed around $47 billion

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.650
in military aid to Ukraine,
the most of any country,

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.263
followed by the EU and the United Kingdom.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.740
The extent to which this aid can continue

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:19.110
at the rate it has been doing recently

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:23.310
is unknown at this point
and in a lengthy war.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.140
Some Western backers of Ukraine

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:28.410
worry that time may be on Russia's side.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.580
- I mean, it looks likely now

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.140
that this is gonna be a long war.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.090
The Russians are gonna end up as sort of,

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.280
you know, suffering long-term damage.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.040
Their military has been
absolutely decimated.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.990
And the Ukrainians, of
course, have lost so much.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.670
So neither side looks like

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.794
it's gonna come out of this war ahead.

00:06:44.794 --> 00:06:47.211
(soft music)

